  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: bonding: alb: fix UAF in rlb_arp_recv during bond up/down (CVE-2026-45970)\n  * kernel: gfs2: Fix slab-use-after-free in qd_put (CVE-2026-45861)\n  * kernel: gfs2: add some missing log locking (CVE-2026-53049)\n  * kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)\n  * kernel: fscrypt: Add missing superblock check in find_or_insert_direct_key() (CVE-2026-68148)\n  * kernel: net: bridge: stop fast-leave after deleting a port group (CVE-2026-74480)\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)\n  * kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n  * kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)\n  * kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n  * kernel: arm64: ptrace: Keep 'orig_x0' in-sync with x0 on syscall entry (CVE-2026-90347)\n  * kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)\n  * kernel: kernel: arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds stack access in scsi_cdl_enable() (CVE-2026-98232)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * netfilter: cve backports for 9.9 (JIRA:RHEL-252129)\n  * Backport the printk SMP startup fix [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-290042)\n  * [IBM 9.10 FEAT] Switch SIGP to always use external call instead of emergency signal [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-303481)\n  * Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-286163)\n  * The Kernel panic occurred at strlen+0x0 because a race event filter treats the user space pointer as a normal pointer [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-291142)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
